From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eicke Hecht <eicke.hecht@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:49:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: zynqmp: spl: boot from boot.bin again after a golden
 image fallback

When boot.bin's boot header is invalid, the boot ROM's golden image
search boots the next image (on SD: BOOT0001.BIN, ...) and leaves its
offset in CSU MULTI_BOOT. The register is only cleared by a power-on
reset, so every later system reset boots the fallback image again, even
after boot.bin has been replaced. Clear it once SPL has loaded U-Boot.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm/mach-zynqmp/spl.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-zynqmp/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-zynqmp/spl.c
index 3e25c88..ec8b8ce 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-zynqmp/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-zynqmp/spl.c
@@ -144,6 +144,15 @@ u32 spl_boot_device(void)
 void spl_board_prepare_for_boot(void)
 {
 	setbits_le32(&pmu_base->gen_storage5, BIT(0) | BIT(1));
+
+	/*
+	 * The boot ROM's golden image search leaves the offset of the image
+	 * it booted in CSU MULTI_BOOT (on SD: n for BOOT000n.BIN), and the
+	 * register keeps it across system resets: after one fallback, every
+	 * later reset would boot that image again, never boot.bin. This one
+	 * has loaded U-Boot, so start the next search at boot.bin again.
+	 */
+	writel(0, &csu_base->multi_boot);
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SPL_OS_BOOT
